# Gameplay Runtime Patterns

- New pot gameplay rules go into validators or processors first, then get called from `PotActions`.
- New day-cycle steps go into dedicated processors/builders first, then get orchestrated by `DayCycleController`.
- Do not add new heavy logic directly to `PotActions` or `DayCycleController` unless it is only a thin delegation layer.
- Cache repeated component lookups in `Awake`, `Start`, or `OnEnable`; do not perform repeated `GetComponent` lookups inside `Update`/`OnGUI` paths unless required.
- If a runtime dependency is needed by multiple systems, register it once and resolve it from `ServiceContainer`.
- If you need all pots or all related controllers, read them from `DomePotRegistry` instead of scanning the scene.
